#!/usr/bin/env bash
# rex-context: point to the installed guides; no private API cache or background refresh.
set -euo pipefail
command -v rex >/dev/null || exit 0
cat <<'EOF'
Rex and teerex provide their own command guides. Read them before operating a pane:
- Rex guide: rex __internal skill
- teerex commands: teerex --help
- Named-host commands: teerex --config ~/.config/teerex/hosts.json --host hive <command> (use --host m5 for the Mac)
- Read a terminal: teerex observe; wait for a change: teerex watch
Use teerex surfaces for pane operations. A missing verb is a teerex gap, not a reason to build plumbing.
Rex says "block" for what agent messaging calls a "pane"; the ids are the same.
EOF
